{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 120, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 5 removed, edge 4 becomes one of the few paths to the output, so upgrading it to a 3x3 conv matters more."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0 is none, node 1 carries zero features, so a conv on edge 1->2 has nothing to process and its benefit vanishes."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 5 is already none leaves the output fed only via edge 4, collapsing the cell and hurting accuracy more."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest op (3x3 conv) with parameter-free pooling loses more than replacing skip, 1x1 conv, or none."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed gives a larger gain than swapping out an existing conv1x1 or avg_pool."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none activates the entire node-1 branch, a bigger gain than upgrading an existing skip connection."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 2 is none, edge 1 is node 2's sole input, so its operation determines node 2's features entirely."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a skip on edge 3, a skip on edge 4 supplies a needed near-residual shortcut to the output; with edge 3 skip it is redundant."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 1 while edge 2 is none disconnects node 2 entirely, wasting edge 5 and shrinking the effective cell."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the valuable input-to-output residual skip with a conv is worse than filling an empty edge 3 with a conv."}], "tok": 30672, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "none"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none